# AI Project Memory

> This file is maintained by TransferLoop. It gives a new AI conversation durable project context plus a short recent history of changes actually accepted into the local project.

## Project Overview

**Project:** gpt themes

gpt themes is a software project managed with TransferLoop. No custom project description has been entered yet; inspect the current files for authoritative implementation details.

## Technical Snapshot

- Primary technologies detected: JavaScript
- Top-level folders: assets, content, options, popup, shared

## Current Direction

- Maintain GPT Themes as a native-page-first cosmetic extension, adapting to ChatGPT DOM changes with narrow resilient selectors instead of replacing native UI.
- Track current ChatGPT component-level native variables in addition to older surface tokens; prefer scoped token compatibility over broad repainting.
- Use live computed-style/paint traces to identify actual ChatGPT painters before adding compatibility overrides; avoid selector/token guesses when the live DOM can be measured.

## Architecture & Important Decisions

- v0.8.14 treats form[data-type='unified-composer'] as the current primary composer while retaining older composer fallbacks.
- Sidebar styling targets known expanded, collapsed, and popover roots rather than generic aside elements.
- User-message transparency is scoped to actual message-bubble surfaces so attachments and file cards retain their native surfaces.
- Current ChatGPT composer theming should target the explicit data-composer-surface shell rather than globally overriding native border tokens.
- Transient menus and command pickers must be fully opaque; support the browser Popover API (:popover-open) as well as semantic/Radix fallbacks.
- Main-surface transparency for image-backed themes should be scoped to the chat canvas rather than applied globally to every main-surface utility class.
- Transient ChatGPT menus must use a guaranteed opaque elevated-surface color even when the active theme intentionally makes chat or assistant surfaces transparent.
- The injected 'Filter visible projects' feature has been removed from GPT Themes.
- Current ChatGPT + and slash-command menus are protected by a targeted runtime menu-surface guard rather than broad generic popover styling.
- The menu guard applies opacity and elevated-surface colors directly to the detected live menu container with inline !important priority.
- Map the current ChatGPT --sidebar-bg token to theme.sidebarBg and reinforce it on known sidebar roots so the entire expanded sidebar uses one continuous configured surface.
- The transient menu-surface detector must explicitly exclude ChatGPT sidebar roots and structural navigation rails before applying cgpt-ui-menu-surface.

## Constraints & Conventions

- Preserve native ChatGPT behavior and avoid broad selectors or native CSS-variable overrides that can unintentionally restyle Work, menus, cards, dialogs, or future controls.
- Do not recolor the already-correct ChatGPT/New chat header block to match an accidental elevated-surface fallback; fix the sidebar body token instead.
- Do not change the working opaque + and slash-command menu treatment while fixing sidebar false positives.

## Open Work

- Live-test v0.8.14 across Chat, Work, collapsed sidebar, mobile/narrow popover sidebar, long pasted drafts, and messages with file attachments after import.
- Live-test v0.8.16 with the + menu and slash-command menu open, then verify the composer edge remains subtle across saved themes and image-backed themes.
- Live-test v0.8.17 with both the + menu and slash-command menu open; if any specific transient surface still escapes the native elevated-token guard, capture that open menu DOM for targeted follow-up.
- Live-test v0.8.18 with both the + menu and slash-command menu; if either remains transparent, use the captured live menu-surface report to identify the exact remaining painted layer.
- Live-test v0.8.22 with the expanded sidebar and confirm the header and scrollable sidebar body now use one continuous surface color.
- Live-test v0.8.23 and confirm the expanded sidebar scrollport no longer receives cgpt-ui-menu-surface and the full sidebar remains one continuous color.
- After v0.8.24 import, verify native ChatGPT wordmark at upper left, collapsed/sidebar-popover layouts, chat-only background offsets, Chat/Work, and +/slash-command menus on the live September browser UI.

## Project Notes

- A passive diagnostic is available in the page context as CgptUiEnhancer.getCompatibilityReport() to help identify future selector drift.
- The supplied September 2026 ChatGPT snapshot shows form[data-type=unified-composer] containing a stable data-composer-surface element and native popover attributes in the current UI.
- Current ChatGPT dark-mode shadow-short-composer includes a light inset shadow; GPT Themes should replace that effect when applying a custom composer surface.
- Current ChatGPT touch-optimized menus use --bg-elevated-primary; mapping that native elevated token to chatAreaBg can make menus transparent in image-backed themes.
- Current menu variants can expose native .__menu-item rows even when ARIA menu roles or earlier Radix content attributes are absent on the painted surface.
- v0.8.18 exposes CgptUiEnhancer.inspectOpenMenus() and includes the last live menu-surface report in compatibility diagnostics for future ChatGPT DOM drift.
- Current ChatGPT expanded sidebar builds can use --sidebar-bg with a fallback to --bg-elevated-secondary, while the sticky header still uses sidebar-surface-primary.
- The live paint trace proved the sidebar mismatch was caused by GPT Themes: the scrollport nav inside #stage-slideover-sidebar was falsely marked cgpt-ui-menu-surface and painted #2f2f2f while the actual sidebar surfaces were correctly #171717.
- The September 26, 2026 ChatGPT browser snapshot uses #app-shell-sidebar inside aside.app-shell-left-panel, and a fixed main header[data-app-shell-titlebar=true] spanning the entire viewport. Theme header painting must leave its left-panel portion transparent when the native sidebar is expanded so the existing native ChatGPT wordmark remains visible.
- The September 28, 2026 ChatGPT fenced-code renderer uses data-markdown-copy="code-block" and may render code directly inside a scrollport with no <pre> element. Treat that semantic data attribute as the primary fenced-code surface and retain pre-based handling only as a legacy fallback.
- Do not apply generic background-color rules to every .markdown code element: in the current renderer that paints a narrow code-row strip inside the fenced-code shell. Paint the semantic code-block shell and keep its descendant code/pre surfaces transparent instead.

## Important Memory Rules

- Current project files are authoritative if this memory ever becomes stale.
- Change-history entries below describe changes accepted through TransferLoop, not merely changes an AI proposed.
- AI assistants should not modify this file during normal implementation work unless the user explicitly asks them to.

